* NAME.COM - CHANGE A NAMED DIRECTORY

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* NAME.COM - CHANGE A NAMED DIRECTORY

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    SYSUTLS:NAME [du:|dir:][newname] [password]

Changes a named-directory table entry. Supplying only a location and
omitting the new name deletes that entry; do not use a bare invocation as
a harmless listing request. Use SYSUTLS:PWD for inspection.

This NAME.COM program is distinct from typing an existing NAME: to select
a directory. NDSCAN can rebuild the table from directory marker files, so
a manual table edit may not survive a refresh. Never publish directory
passwords in help examples.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
